/**
 * Compliance hub. Deliberately NOT a thin index — it carries its own substance:
 * everything a Texas customer is entitled to receive, see, check and keep, with
 * the rule behind each one. All verified Aug 2026 via Cornell LII / Justia
 * mirrors of 4 TAC ch. 7 subchapter H.
 *
 *  §7.141(a)  licensee must CARRY the licence card at all times when working
 *  §7.141(b)  must present credentials on request
 *  §7.141(c)  must present GOVERNMENT PHOTO ID to a customer on request  ← gem
 *  §7.141(d)  business licence available at the place of business
 *  §7.141(g)-(h) vehicle must display "Texas Pest Control License #" or
 *             "TPCL #" permanently affixed to front fenders or door panels,
 *             letters at least TWO INCHES tall, contrasting colours
 *  §7.145(a)  jurisdiction statement + business name, licence number, address
 *             and phone on the face of every contract, warranty, service
 *             agreement, termite disclosure document or guarantee
 *  §7.145(b)  business name, licence number, phone, address on every INVOICE
 *  §7.145(c)  both must be legible and in at least 8-POINT TYPE
 *  §7.144(a)  pest control use records kept TWO YEARS at the business facility,
 *             including pesticide names AND EPA registration numbers, total
 *             amounts applied, mixing rate, target pest, date, applicator name
 *             and licence number, and the business TPCL number
 *  §7.144(c)  those records available to TDA on written OR VERBAL request
 *  §7.123     insurance: not less than $500,000 bodily injury and property
 *             damage, minimum $1,000,000 total annual aggregate; 30 days'
 *             notice to the department before cancellation; carrier must notify
 *             within 10 business days if claims drop the aggregate below $1M
 *  §7.177     WDI inspection sticker on the wall adjacent to the water heater,
 *             electric breaker box, or beneath the kitchen sink
 *  §7.172(d)  post-construction termite treatment sticker, not less than
 *             1in x 2in, same locations
 *
 * HOME SOLICITATION — CORRECTED. TDA's own consumer sheet says "72 hours".
 * The governing statute, Bus. & Com. Code §601.052, says "AT ANY TIME PRIOR TO
 * MIDNIGHT OF THE THIRD BUSINESS DAY AFTER THE DATE OF THIS TRANSACTION" in
 * boldfaced type of at least 10 points. Third business day is NOT 72 hours over
 * a weekend. This page publishes the statutory language, not the shorthand.
 */
